                "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                "username": "dkodihal"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2: Code-Review+1"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1773337741,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n-"
        },
        {
            "timestamp": 1773337871,
            "reviewer": {
                "name": "garybeihl",
                "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                "username": "garybeihl"
            },
            "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\nI'd like to work on a d-bus interface follow-up that will be included in the next patchset of this change.\n\nIt looks like BoardIntf is a pure marker interface  none of the property setters (partNumber,\nserialNumber, etc.) delegate to it; they all go through the decorator interfaces (Asset, AssetTag,\n Revision, Compatible). So let's replace the compile-time BoardIntf inheritance with a\n runtime-selected Item interface using type erasure (ItemIntfBase + ItemIntfHolder<T>).\n The PldmEntityReq constructor takes the entityType and a factory method selects the correct\n Inventory.Item.* interface. No changes would be needed to the property setter logic.\n\nThe mapping would be:\n Board/SysBoard/Card => Item.Board\n System Chassis => Item.Chassis\n Processor => Item.Cpu\n GPU/Accelerator => Item.Accelerator\n Memory Module => Item.Dimm\n Fan => Item.Fan\n Power Supply => Item.PowerSupply\n Unknown/default => Item.Board"
        },
