            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "The D-Bus interface on these objects will still be a common set (including Board). Is there also a plan to add relevant interfaces based on the entity type? Or is this limited to fixing the human-readability of these paths?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "garybeihl",
                        "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "garybeihl"
                    },
                    "message": "See my comment below"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "garybeihl",
                        "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "garybeihl"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Deepak \u2014 I've completed the entity-type-specific D-Bus interface changes you asked about. I refactored PldmEntityReq from a concrete class inheriting Board to a template parameterized by the Item interface type (e.g. PldmEntityReq<cpuserver> for processors). A PldmEntityBase abstract base class provides the property setters via Decorator interfaces, and a createPldmEntity() factory function selects the correct template instantiation based on PLDM entity type. Mapped types are: Accelerator (GPU), Cpu, Dimm, Fan, PowerSupply, Chassis, Board (default).\n\nWould you prefer this folded into this change as PS3, or as a separate follow-up?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "A separate follow-up please. Thanks for completing this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "garybeihl",
                        "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "garybeihl"
                    },
                    "message": "I pushed the follow-up D-bus interface changes to a new PR 89127 \u2014 https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/pldm/+/89127 - please review when you get a chance."
                }
            ],
